s of acid or base.\nL52: 【23†Application:】  | 【24†renoprotective agent】  Any compound that is able to prevent damage to the kidneys.\nL53: \nL54: ChEBI Ontology\nL55: ---\nL56: \nL57: Text\nL58: \nL59: Tree View\nL60: \nL61: Graph View\nL62: Outgoing Relation(s)\nL63: dipotassium hydrogen phosphate (【25†CHEBI:131527】) has role buffer (【22†CHEBI:35225】)\nL64: dipotassium hydrogen phosphate (【25†CHEBI:131527】) has role renoprotective agent (【24†CHEBI:231911】)\nL65: dipotassium hydrogen phosphate (【25†CHEBI:131527】) is a inorganic phosphate (【26†CHEBI:24838】)\nL66: dipotassium hydrogen phosphate (【25†CHEBI:131527】) is a potassium salt (【27†CHEBI:26218】)\nL67: \nL68: IUPAC Name\nL69: ---\nL70: dipotassium hydrogen phosphate\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\npotassium dihydrogen phosphate (CHEBI:63036) (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A63036 ; rewritten summary of https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:63036)\nciteturn5view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:63036\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:63036; Total lines: 96\nL0:   * 【0†Advanced Search】\nL1:   * 【1†Submit】\nL2:   * 【2†Downloads】\nL3:   * 【3†Tools】\nL4:   * 【4†Docs】\nL5:   * 【5†About】\nL6:   * 【6†Contact】\nL7: \nL8: 【7†EMBL-EBI†ebi.ac.uk】 | 【8†Chemical Biology Resources】 | 【9†ChEBI】\nL9: \nL10: Search[Input: Enter your search term]\nL11: \nL12: Search\nL13: \nL14: Example searches: 【10†iron*】, 【11†InChI=1S/CH4O/c1-2/h2H,1H3】, 【12†caffeine】 | 【0†Advanced Search】\nL15: ## CHEBI:63036 - potassium dihydrogen phosphate\nL16: \nL17: 【13†Image: Default Structure】\nL18: \nL19: Take structure to advanced search\nL20: \nL21: ChEBI ID  | CHEBI:63036\nL22: ChEBI Name  | potassium dihydrogen phosphate\nL23: Stars  |\nL24: Definition  | A potassium salt in which dihydrogen phosphate(1−) is the counterion.\nL25: Last Modified  | 2 April 2020\nL26: Submitt