reaction that donates an electron to another species.\nL51: 【23†Application:】  | 【24†bleaching agent】  A reagent that lightens or whitens a substrate through chemical reaction. Bleaching reactions usually involve oxidative or reductive processes that degrade colour systems. Bleaching can occur by destroying one or more of the double bonds in the conjugated chain, by cleaving the conjugated chain, or by oxidation of one of the other moieties in the conjugated chain.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nsodium molybdate dihydrate (CHEBI:75213) (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A75213 ; rewritten summary of https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:75213)\nciteturn5view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:75213\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:75213; Total lines: 90\nL0:   * 【0†Advanced Search】\nL1:   * 【1†Submit】\nL2:   * 【2†Downloads】\nL3:   * 【3†Tools】\nL4:   * 【4†Docs】\nL5:   * 【5†About】\nL6:   * 【6†Contact】\nL7: \nL8: 【7†EMBL-EBI†ebi.ac.uk】 | 【8†Chemical Biology Resources】 | 【9†ChEBI】\nL9: \nL10: Search[Input: Enter your search term]\nL11: \nL12: Search\nL13: \nL14: Example searches: 【10†iron*】, 【11†InChI=1S/CH4O/c1-2/h2H,1H3】, 【12†caffeine】 | 【0†Advanced Search】\nL15: ## CHEBI:75213 - sodium molybdate dihydrate\nL16: \nL17: 【13†Image: Default Structure】\nL18: \nL19: Take structure to advanced search\nL20: \nL21: ChEBI ID  | CHEBI:75213\nL22: ChEBI Name  | sodium molybdate dihydrate\nL23: Stars  |\nL24: Definition  | A hydrate that is the dihydrate form of sodium molybdate.\nL25: Last Modified  | 26 February 2024\nL26: Submitter  | Steve\nL27: Downloads  | 【14†Molfile】\nL28: \nL29: On this page\nL30: \nL31:   * 【15†Intro】\nL32:   * 【16†Roles Classification】\nL33:   * 【17†Ontology】\nL34:   * 【18†Names】\nL35:   * 【19†Manual Xrefs】\nL36:   * 【20†Registry Numbers】\nL37:   * 【21†Citations】\nL38: Form